    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` on the owner read model so it returns `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` (built at compile time by the openapi-generator) carries the field.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when `email` is non-null/non-blank, else `\"PHONE\"`. This mirrors the existing derived-field pattern (`getMembershipLevel()`), and MapStruct auto-maps it into the DTO by property name \u2014 no mapper changes needed.\n\nThe change follows the repo's established idiom for derived owner fields, and both acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) plus the whole suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
